    {
      "id": "4231c655-4214-4155-a2a4-abec21d3c09d",
      "label": "*weyd- (PIE see)",
      "aliases": [],
      "type": "concept",
      "description": "# Semantic Evolution\n\nThe connection between *weyd- and the Proto-Celtic *windos (\"white\") relies on a specific semantic shift:\n\nOriginal Meaning: \"To see\" or \"to perceive.\"\nDerived Meaning: \"To be seen\" or \"visible.\"\nFinal Shift: \"Bright,\" \"shining,\" or \"white\" (that which is clearly seen). \nLinguists reconstruct *windos as potentially deriving from a nasal-infix form of this root (*windo-), suggesting a conceptual link where \"white\" is defined as \"that which is most visible\" or \"bright.\" \n\n-- https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Celtic/windos\n\n-- https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/weyd-\n\nSynonym: dark? https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/der%E1%B8%B1-",
      "tags": [],
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T11:49:45.957Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T11:54:51.174Z"
    },
